driguez, 2008). This study covers the territory of the Autonomous Region of Madrid. This small Region of only 8.021,80 km2 constitutes an excellent physical framework for the practical study of the concept «sustainable development». It is the most densely populated Region in Spain (757 inhabitants/km2). It has one of the highest densities of infrastructures of the country and a thriving economy, often opposed to habitats and species’ conservation objectives (Rodriguez, 2008). It also enjoys one of the highest income levels of Spain, with (28.064 €/inh.). As of August 2008, there exist 10 PAs declared in the Region of Madrid. They occupy some 110,000 ha., which represents nearly 14% of the Region’s surface.","citation":"David Rodríguez (2009)","page":"1"}
