rg/W1972123129","https://openalex.org/W2022799863","https://openalex.org/W2060528447","https://openalex.org/W2069226769","https://openalex.org/W2072643567","https://openalex.org/W2075777258","https://openalex.org/W2102959794","https://openalex.org/W2103247577","https://openalex.org/W2103585535","https://openalex.org/W2247790751","https://openalex.org/W2249716455","https://openalex.org/W2261592960","https://openalex.org/W2336312874","https://openalex.org/W3041729887","https://openalex.org/W3097304711"],"related_works":["https://openalex.org/W2130966585","https://openalex.org/W2152277279","https://openalex.org/W1971745830","https://openalex.org/W2235830263","https://openalex.org/W2099936079","https://openalex.org/W2114184350","https://openalex.org/W2275715063","https://openalex.org/W3038998520","https://openalex.org/W2105709334","https://openalex.org/W2029649049","https://openalex.org/W1997525514","https://openalex.org/W2001017918","https://openalex.org/W1988759648","https://openalex.org/W2508092388","https://openalex.org/W1993349214","https://openalex.org/W2080918200","https://openalex.org/W2072538579","https://openalex.org/W2067784200","https://openalex.org/W38980906","https://openalex.org/W2148996375"],"counts_by_year":[],"updated_date":"2026-10-13T10:08:12.033832","created_date":"2025-10-10T00:00:00","abstract":"The fjords and inner waters present in the south of Chile constitute an area of great ecological and zoogeographical interest. In the year 2004 were carried out an investigation project about biodiversity as part of the CIMAR 10 Fiordos cruise, organized and financed by the National Oceanographic Committee of Chile (CONA) that allowed the obtaining of subtidal samples of molluscs in the northern end of the Magellanic Province. In this study we present an analysis of the composition, diversity and space distribution of the molluscan fauna obtained in the cruise. A total of 23 sites, distributed among the Seno Reloncavi (41o 31' S) and the Boca del Guafo (43o 99' S) were sampled. The samples were obtained using an Agassiz trawl (of 10 mm of mesh; sampling 10 minutes), to depths among 22 353 m. A total of 67 species were recorded, consistent in 4% Polyplacophora, 58% Gastropoda, 36% Bivalvia and 1% Scaphopoda. The results show that the subtidal species have a high proportion of species with southern features, characteristic of the Magellanic Province. The multivariate analyses allowed to recognize six areas inside the studied territory, clearly recognizable for their composition and species richness.","citation":"Claudio Valdovinos et al. (2008)","page":"1"}
