],"has_content":{"pdf":false,"grobid_xml":false},"content_urls":null,"referenced_works_count":0,"referenced_works":[],"related_works":["https://openalex.org/W2523164519","https://openalex.org/W2746064605","https://openalex.org/W2086761216","https://openalex.org/W2022499692","https://openalex.org/W185606074","https://openalex.org/W3126120129","https://openalex.org/W1992868415","https://openalex.org/W2794563620","https://openalex.org/W3151092703","https://openalex.org/W1937694480","https://openalex.org/W3094474868","https://openalex.org/W3087660247","https://openalex.org/W2079322498","https://openalex.org/W3008378145","https://openalex.org/W2948453386","https://openalex.org/W1546008044","https://openalex.org/W791576140","https://openalex.org/W2057895624","https://openalex.org/W3133163008","https://openalex.org/W1999012314"],"counts_by_year":[],"updated_date":"2025-11-06T04:12:42.849631","created_date":"2025-10-10T00:00:00","abstract":"Against a backdrop of increasing attention to social assessment and participation issues throughout the World Bank and within the Global Environment Facility (GEF), the Bank's Global Environment Coordination Division (ENVGC) conducted a retrospective review of stakeholder identification and participation in the portfolio of projects financed by the GEF. The review covered 72 GEF-financed projects currently in the Bank's work program. Specifically, 41 biodiversity conservation projects, 22 climate change mitigation projects, 6 international waters projects, and 3 ozone projection projects were reviewed. The review took stock of the treatment of stakeholder identification and participation issues in the GEF portfolio as measured over time, cataloged both constraints to and support for participation, and gleaned lessons and good practice tips that can be applied to on-going and future activities. The quantitative data showed that projects are addressing stakeholder participation more systematically and more effectively over time. Qualitative data revealed some of the ways in which GEF-financed projects are supporting participatory approaches. In addition, good practice tips for encouraging and supporting systematic stakeholder identification and participation are emerging through project experience.","citation":"Maria Aycrigg (1997)","page":"1"}
