ated_date":"2025-10-10T00:00:00","abstract":"This report focuses on the achievements of forestry pastoral Project (RISEMP) in the pilot area of Costa Rica. Specifically, it focuses on the effect of the payment on the changes described in land use introduced by farmers, monitoring results of the present generation of environmental services, carbon sequestration and biodiversity increase in applications of the most predominant soil in the landscape. Study results also show that in the project area it was evident that water is a scarce resource and that the generation of the service was rebranded as being as very important to the people of the area. Finally, it compares the payment schemes corresponding to the currently RISEMP employed by the Payment for Ecosystem Services (PES) implemented by the National Forestry Financing Fund (FONAFIFO).","citation":"Cristóbal Villanueva et al. (2007)","page":"1"}
