ll,"version":null,"is_accepted":false,"is_published":null,"raw_source_name":null,"raw_type":null}],"best_oa_location":null,"sustainable_development_goals":[{"score":0.9599999785423279,"id":"https://metadata.un.org/sdg/15","display_name":"Life on land"},{"score":0.8787999749183655,"id":"https://metadata.un.org/sdg/11","display_name":"Sustainable cities and communities"},{"score":0.6773999929428101,"id":"https://metadata.un.org/sdg/9","display_name":"Industry, innovation and infrastructure"},{"score":0.4399999976158142,"id":"https://metadata.un.org/sdg/13","display_name":"Climate action"}],"sustainable_development_goals_aurora":[{"score":0.6200000047683716,"id":"https://metadata.un.org/sdg/15","display_name":"Life on land"}],"study_designs":[],"awards":[],"funders":[],"has_content":{"pdf":false,"grobid_xml":false},"content_urls":null,"referenced_works_count":0,"referenced_works":[],"related_works":["https://openalex.org/W616578219","https://openalex.org/W158349700","https://openalex.org/W1865935121","https://openalex.org/W354899234","https://openalex.org/W212386611","https://openalex.org/W568918617","https://openalex.org/W185137466","https://openalex.org/W261970524","https://openalex.org/W1875042455","https://openalex.org/W650910070","https://openalex.org/W582866422","https://openalex.org/W175543040","https://openalex.org/W363500558","https://openalex.org/W2584877168","https://openalex.org/W374785462","https://openalex.org/W313648888","https://openalex.org/W1597436908","https://openalex.org/W260845328","https://openalex.org/W1201594141","https://openalex.org/W2560792761"],"counts_by_year":[],"updated_date":"2026-09-29T14:09:16.559479","created_date":"2025-10-10T00:00:00","abstract":"The Rural Access Roads Project will improve accessibility to social, communal, and administrative services, thus improving the rural way of life. Although environmental impacts resulting from project implementation, are expected to be limited - the project will not finance activities related to deforestation, adversity on natural habitats, or biodiversity, nor on cultural sites - this environmental assessment identifies adverse impacts mainly during construction, and takes into consideration Morocco's legal and regulatory framework, to form the basis for the following mitigation measures. Natural habitats and biodiversity will be avoided, establishing protected areas limiting construction sites. Similarly, soil erosion and potential landslides would be avoided, taking into consideration adequate stable soils, and establishing drainage systems in areas prone to floods, while excavations should be limited during the dry season only. Oil spills, and lubricants should be handled and disposed of in accordance with standard regulations, storage procedures, and waste management best practices. To minimize air and noise pollution, re-vegetation and tree planting along the roads would form protective barriers limiting dust emissions, and noise disturbances.","citation":"Morocco (2004)","page":"1"}
